## What Problem This Solves

Tool Search cannot measure terminology-mismatch opportunities among its authorized lexical results without changing which tools it selects.

## User Impact

Adds default-off `tools.toolSearch.semanticRanking: "shadow"` under the shared Decision assistance Labs gate and the owning agent's explicit Decision model. It records semantic comparison counters but returns the original lexical results; exact-name selection avoids Decision. Visibility, limits, schemas and execution authority remain unchanged.

The budget is cooperative: Tool Search joins already-started provider work, so an abort-ignoring provider may exceed it. No ranking-quality, latency or cost benefit is claimed. Consumer inclusion and this latency tradeoff remain owner decisions, not claimed approvals.

## Why This Change Was Made

One observer covers structured Tool Search and its actual Code Mode bridge, evaluating at most eight already-returnable descriptors without parameter schemas. Errors preserve lexical results; cancellation joins admitted work; catalog state is revalidated after awaits.

The current review repair reads current shadow mode, Tool Search enabled state and shared Labs/model eligibility on retained controls. Its owner-bound eligibility callback also reaches the Decision host's final provider-admission boundary after asynchronous Gateway authority preparation. The Decision runtime captures its config owner before that preparation and rechecks selected-model identity immediately before dispatch, so replacing a nonempty model also prevents dispatch to the old model. Explicit Decision calls remain independent of consumer Labs gating. Tool factories preserve their original mutable context identities, which own catalog/guest lifetimes, while retaining the config reader.

