Follow-up to #158354.

If deferred terminal publication throws after the update run has already been durably finalized as `succeeded`, the outer unexpected-failure path currently treats it like a pending recovery and can print `Update recovery remains pending`.

The ledger is already authoritative at that point. This change:
- re-reads the finalized run before unexpected-failure admission;
- if it is already `succeeded`, reports the publication failure explicitly;
- exits through the existing `UpdateCommandFinalizedRecoveryFailure` reporting-only marker;
- does not relabel the durable update outcome or offer recovery triage.

The existing completed-publication regression now asserts that the publication failure is visible and pending-recovery wording is absent.

